WEBVTT

00:06:28.916 --> 00:06:30.916
they get understandably suspicious.

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:33.596
Because historically,
it's been an excuse for inaction.

00:06:33.596 --> 00:06:36.636
We can continue polluting,
and we’ll clean up later.

00:06:36.676 --> 00:06:38.396
You're telling us in your view

00:06:38.436 --> 00:06:41.156
that carbon removals
are an imperative piece of the plan.

00:06:41.156 --> 00:06:43.476
Can you describe why
and what you mean by that?

00:06:43.476 --> 00:06:45.916
RP: Of course. I mean,
people should be suspicious.

00:06:45.916 --> 00:06:47.956
Carbon removal needs to be the last piece.

00:06:47.956 --> 00:06:50.796
So as an organization,
if you're trying to get to net-zero,

00:06:50.796 --> 00:06:53.316
the first thing
you have to do is cut, right?

00:06:53.316 --> 00:06:56.316
Pick the alternative,
pick the electric alternative.

00:06:56.356 --> 00:06:58.116
Then you’ve got to be more efficient.

00:06:58.156 --> 00:07:00.236
So you've got to cut,
become more efficient,